## Aralsk-7 (Vozrozhdeniya Island): The Bioweapons Proving Ground

In **1954**, the Soviet Ministry of Defense established a super-secret ultra-restricted military facility in the absolute center of the Aral Sea on Vozrozhdeniya Island ("Rebirth Island"): **Aralsk-7**:
* **The Perfect Island Crucible:** Geographically isolated by hundreds of kilometers of water, sparsely populated, and cursed with arid heat that quickly degrades organic matter, the island was the ideal laboratory for open-air field-testing of genetic bioweapons.
* **Kantubek Ghost City:** A closed military settlement housing 1,500 scientists, officers, and their families was built on the island, complete with schools, barracks, cinemas, laboratories, and an expansive multi-runway airfield (Barkhan).
* **The Aerosol Kill-Grid:** On open-air artillery ranges south of Kantubek, Soviet military doctors tied hundreds of caged horses, sheep, baboons, and guinea pigs to wooden posts. Aircraft flew overhead at low altitudes, releasing aerosolized mists of genetically engineered **Bacillus anthracis (Anthrax)**, **Yersinia pestis (Bubonic Plague)**, **Francisella tularensis (Tularemia)**, and **Smallpox**. Telemetry stations monitored kill rates, dispersal patterns, and wind vectors across miles of open flats.

