## The Verdict

The Aral Sea and Vozrozhdeniya Island stand as the 20th century’s most profound monument to human hubris. Standing among the skeletal, sand-choked hulls of Moynaq as wind whips salt across the desert floor, travelers gaze upon an entire sea murdered by bureaucratic ambition—a silent, sun-bleached graveyard where water turned to dust, and where the darkest secrets of military science sleep beneath the dunes.
